@startuml
title A sanctioned holder tries to move their own tokens

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam activityBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam activityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam activityDiamondBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #4A78B5

start
:Sanctioned holder signs a transaction
spending their own programmable-base UTxO
carrying the security token;<<#EEF5FF>>
:CIP-113 base layer gates the spend
and dispatches [TransferAct];<<#EEF5FF>>
note right
  The holder owns the UTxO, so owner
  consent is satisfied. Consent is not
  the gate that stops this transfer.
end note
:transfer_logic_validator.withdraw runs;<<#EEF5FF>>
:Authenticate GlobalState by its NFT
at the redeemer's GlobalStateLocation;<<#EEF5FF>>

if (Sender address has an inline stake credential?) then (no)
  :REJECTED - validator traps
  enterprise addresses are not
  owners under CIP-113;<<#FDEEEE>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:Aggregate unique SENDER credentials from
inputs carrying the token, and unique
DESTINATION credentials from outputs;<<#EEF5FF>>

if (transfers_paused?) then (yes)
  :REJECTED;<<#FDEEEE>>
  stop
else (no)
endif
if (deactivated?) then (yes)
  :REJECTED;<<#FDEEEE>>
  stop
else (no)
endif

partition "verify_parties - sender side" {
  :Each sender must supply a covering-node
  reference input from the denylist;<<#EEF5FF>>
  note right
    A covering node proves ABSENCE:
    covering_key < target < covering_link.
    Both bounds are STRICT, and the node
    must sit at denylist_script_hash.
  end note
  if (Node keyed exactly at this hash present?) then (yes - the sanction)
    :REJECTED
    no covering node can span the target:
    equality fails both strict bounds, so
    the absence proof cannot be built;<<#FDEEEE>>
    stop
  else (no)
  endif
  if (requires_sender_kyc and no valid proof?) then (yes)
    :REJECTED;<<#FDEEEE>>
    stop
  else (no)
  endif
}

partition "verify_parties - destination side" {
  if (Destination denylisted, or KYC missing when required?) then (yes)
    :REJECTED
    presence blocks RECEIVING too;<<#FDEEEE>>
    stop
  else (no)
  endif
}

:Transfer accepted;<<#EAF6F0>>
stop

note left
  A sanctioned holder never gets here.
  The only way their position moves is
  third_party_transfer_logic_validator,
  the seizure path, which runs no
  source-side checks and requires a
  power user holding can_force_transfer.
end note
@enduml
